[[:db/retract 17592186382208 :answer-field/choices 17592186382209] [:db/retract 17592186382208 :answer-field/choices 17592186382210] [:db/retract 17592186382208 :answer-field/choices 17592186382211] [:db/retract 17592186382208 :answer-field/choices 17592186382212] [:db/retract 17592186382208 :answer-field/choices 17592186382213] [:db/retract 17592186409555 :answer-field/choices 17592186409552] [:db/retract 17592186409555 :answer-field/choices 17592186409539] [:db/retract 17592186409555 :answer-field/choices 17592186409540] [:db/retract 17592186409555 :answer-field/choices 17592186409545] [:db/retract 17592186409555 :answer-field/choices 17592186409547] {:db/id 17592186382207 :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $f(x,y,z)=\\frac{{e}^{\\sqrt{xy}}}{z}$ is defined only when $xy\\ge 0$ and $z\\ne 0.$ So, the domain of $f$ is \n\n$$\n{D}_{f}=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,xy\\ge 0,z\\ne 0\\}.\n$$\n\nAs for the partial derivatives, we have the following.\n\n- The function ${f}_{x}=\\frac{y{e}^{\\sqrt{xy}}}{2z\\sqrt{xy}}$ is defined only when $xy>0$ and $z\\ne 0.$ So, the domain of ${f}_{x}$ is \n\n$$\n{D}_{{f}_{x}}=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,xy>0,z\\ne 0\\}.\n$$\n\n- Similarly, the domain of ${f}_{y}=\\frac{x{e}^{\\sqrt{xy}}}{2z\\sqrt{xy}}$ is the same\n\n$$\n{D}_{{f}_{y}}=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,xy>0,z\\ne 0\\}.\n$$\n\n- The function ${f}_{z}=-\\frac{{e}^{\\sqrt{xy}}}{{z}^{2}}$ is defined only when $xy\\ge 0$ and $z\\ne 0.$ So, the domain of ${f}_{z}$ is\n\n$$\n{D}_{{f}_{z}}=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,xy\\ge 0,z\\ne 0\\}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we conclude that the partials of $f$ exist on the set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{f}\\cap {D}_{{f}_{x}}\\cap {D}_{{f}_{y}}\\cap {D}_{{f}_{z}} & ={D}_{f}\\cap {D}_{{f}_{x}} \\\\  & =\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,xy\\ge 0,z\\ne 0\\}\\cap \\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,xy>0,z\\ne 0\\} \\\\  & =\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,xy>0,z\\ne 0\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186382208 :answer-field/correct "answer-629c6583-5abe-5cd2-8098-b6cded7ee4e3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a318ea21-95fd-5a51-9e1e-c2501bcf0d2e" "answer-395e6ad4-f871-5195-aed0-c82a5612a79c" "answer-629c6583-5abe-5cd2-8098-b6cded7ee4e3" "answer-32e88f5b-98b5-56cf-80ff-82851c3303b7" "answer-410d16c0-a17f-5bb6-8557-36dd6a7c08d7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a318ea21-95fd-5a51-9e1e-c2501bcf0d2e" :answer/id #uuid "a318ea21-95fd-5a51-9e1e-c2501bcf0d2e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,xy=0,z\\ne 0\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-395e6ad4-f871-5195-aed0-c82a5612a79c" :answer/id #uuid "395e6ad4-f871-5195-aed0-c82a5612a79c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,xy>0,z>0\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-629c6583-5abe-5cd2-8098-b6cded7ee4e3" :answer/id #uuid "629c6583-5abe-5cd2-8098-b6cded7ee4e3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,xy>0,z\\ne 0\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-32e88f5b-98b5-56cf-80ff-82851c3303b7" :answer/id #uuid "32e88f5b-98b5-56cf-80ff-82851c3303b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,xy\\ge 0,z\\ne 0\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-410d16c0-a17f-5bb6-8557-36dd6a7c08d7" :answer/id #uuid "410d16c0-a17f-5bb6-8557-36dd6a7c08d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,xy\\ne 0,z<0\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186382221 :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true about the function $f(x,y,z)=\\sqrt{2x+y-z}?$ \n\nI. ${f}_{y}(1,1,1)$ is defined\n\nII. ${f}_{z}(0,1,2)$ is defined\n\nIII. The partial derivative with respect to $x$ is defined at $(0,1,1)$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186409559 :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $f(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xyz)$ is defined only when $xyz>0.$ So, the domain of $f$ is \n\n$$\n{D}_{f}=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,xyz>0\\}.\n$$\n\nAs for the partial derivatives, we have the following.\n\n- The function $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{1}{x}$ is defined only when $x\\ne 0.$ So, the domain of ${f}_{x}$ is \n\n$$\n{D}_{{f}_{x}}=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,x\\ne 0\\}.\n$$\n\n- The function $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\frac{1}{y}$ is defined only when $y\\ne 0.$ So, the domain of ${f}_{y}$ is \n\n$$\n{D}_{{f}_{y}}=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,y\\ne 0\\}.\n$$\n\n- The function $\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=\\frac{1}{z}$ is defined only when $z\\ne 0.$ So, the domain of ${f}_{z}$ is \n\n$$\n{D}_{{f}_{z}}=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,z\\ne 0\\}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we conclude that the partial derivatives of $f$ exist on the set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{f}\\cap {D}_{{f}_{x}}\\cap {D}_{{f}_{y}}\\cap {D}_{{f}_{z}} & =\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,xyz>0\\}\\cap \\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,x\\ne 0\\}\\cap \\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,y\\ne 0\\}\\cap \\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,z\\ne 0\\} \\\\  & =\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,xyz>0\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186409555 :answer-field/correct "answer-603bfd17-5e73-595d-9e4e-67eb66547b83" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b33e9175-1fe3-525c-84d8-993f2fb37971" "answer-6e5cf9f7-9ed5-55ea-b3dd-342a00251b3b" "answer-1625c29f-0f6c-51a9-9abf-da854c690be8" "answer-603bfd17-5e73-595d-9e4e-67eb66547b83" "answer-d2f2980b-11d7-556d-9928-b285bb77ebda"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b33e9175-1fe3-525c-84d8-993f2fb37971" :answer/id #uuid "b33e9175-1fe3-525c-84d8-993f2fb37971" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,x+y+z>0\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6e5cf9f7-9ed5-55ea-b3dd-342a00251b3b" :answer/id #uuid "6e5cf9f7-9ed5-55ea-b3dd-342a00251b3b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,x\\ne 0,\\,y\\ne 0,\\,z\\ne 0\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1625c29f-0f6c-51a9-9abf-da854c690be8" :answer/id #uuid "1625c29f-0f6c-51a9-9abf-da854c690be8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,xyz>0,\\,x+y+z\\ne 0\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-603bfd17-5e73-595d-9e4e-67eb66547b83" :answer/id #uuid "603bfd17-5e73-595d-9e4e-67eb66547b83" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,xyz>0\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d2f2980b-11d7-556d-9928-b285bb77ebda" :answer/id #uuid "d2f2980b-11d7-556d-9928-b285bb77ebda" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,xyz\\ge 0\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186268907 :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true about the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{\\sqrt{x}}{{y}^{2}}?$\n\nI. Both partial derivatives exist at the point $(4,2)$\n\nII. ${f}_{x}(0,2)$ is defined\n\nIII. ${f}_{y}(0,2)$ is defined" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "activity-2432ea49-4693-51cf-9b05-9340c356690d" :activity/id #uuid "2432ea49-4693-51cf-9b05-9340c356690d" :activity/title "Partial Differentiability of Multivariable Functions" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048877 :activity/course 17592186046658 :activity/steps ["step-5c9fcb15-a332-5a35-8e19-9f260bf4cc92" "step-c05be20d-2e9f-5518-9fbb-273892668ed2" "step-1b612f2a-e93c-5ad0-972f-c5368a3312ef" "step-7b68aec1-f3e3-5aa1-bec7-f5fcbb362752" "step-5a19d090-fc30-5d59-972c-c7b1fd1ca305"] :activity/first-step "step-5c9fcb15-a332-5a35-8e19-9f260bf4cc92" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-5c9fcb15-a332-5a35-8e19-9f260bf4cc92" :step/id #uuid "5c9fcb15-a332-5a35-8e19-9f260bf4cc92" :step/content 17592186382207 :step/next "step-c05be20d-2e9f-5518-9fbb-273892668ed2" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-c05be20d-2e9f-5518-9fbb-273892668ed2" :step/id #uuid "c05be20d-2e9f-5518-9fbb-273892668ed2" :step/content 17592186382221 :step/next "step-1b612f2a-e93c-5ad0-972f-c5368a3312ef" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-1b612f2a-e93c-5ad0-972f-c5368a3312ef" :step/id #uuid "1b612f2a-e93c-5ad0-972f-c5368a3312ef" :step/content 17592186409559 :step/next "step-7b68aec1-f3e3-5aa1-bec7-f5fcbb362752" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-7b68aec1-f3e3-5aa1-bec7-f5fcbb362752" :step/id #uuid "7b68aec1-f3e3-5aa1-bec7-f5fcbb362752" :